.TH READ 2 "2026-09-06" "EpinAnonymOS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
read \- Linux syscall 0, as implemented by the EpinAnonymOS kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syscall(0, ...)
.br
kernel handler: \fBlinux_sys_read\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
No implementation notes recorded in the source for this call.  The
call is dispatched and implemented; see IMPLEMENTATION for where, and read the source before
relying on stock Linux semantics.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION
Dispatched from \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/kernel_main.d\fR;
implemented in \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/syscalls/posix.d\fR.
.SH CAVEAT
This kernel emulates a SUBSET of the Linux ABI.  Behaviour that stock Linux
guarantees is not guaranteed here unless the DESCRIPTION says so.  Notably,
AF_UNIX reads return EAGAIN on an empty socket rather than blocking, and
absolute opens are resolved against the calling task's namespace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR anonymos-syscalls (7)
